('P', 'Autism spectrum disorder (ASD) is a lifelong neurodevelopmental condition marked by differences in social communication and by restricted, repetitive patterns of behavior, interests, or sensory response, present from early childhood (American Psychiatric Association [APA], 2022). It ranges from people who need very substantial daily support to independent adults with careers and families.'),
('P', '**How common:** in the U.S., 1 in 36 eight-year-olds (27.6 per 1,000) had ASD in 2020, about 3.8 times more often in boys (Maenner et al., 2023). Worldwide, the median estimate is about 1 in 100, and about one-third of autistic people also have intellectual disability (Zeidan et al., 2022).'),
